            <ArticleTitle>It's not inside, it's on top! - An unusual cause of right iliac fossa pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-56</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rectus sheath haematoma (RSH) is an uncommon cause of acute abdominal pain, but can mimic a variety of acute surgical conditions. Computed tomography (CT) provides the diagnosis and avoids unnecessary procedures.</AbstractText>
